pulled up to the supply (+3V3) so the module runs when reset is not asserted.\",\n      \"evidence\": [\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"U10\\\") (pin \\\"9\\\") (pinfunction \\\"RESET_N\\\") (pintype \\\"input\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"netlist\", \"quote\": \"(node (ref \\\"R38\\\") (pin \\\"1\\\") (pintype \\\"passive\\\"))\"},\n        {\"source\": \"spice\", \"quote\": \"R38 0 GPS_NRST_NAVC 10k\"}\n      ],\n      \"impact\": \"If RESET_N is held low, the GPS receiver stays in reset and produces no navigation data, which would disable GPS on the NAVC side.\",\n      \"confidence\": 0.25\n    }\n  ],\n  \"summary\": \"LED2 has its anode tied to ground rather than the 3.3 V rail, so the status LED cannot light, which is the most clearly supported deviation. The GPS RESET_N pull-down to ground is a lower-confidence second finding.\"\n}",
